{"sourceSha256": "10f5ebb94f74c6633bf28c508dcae3158ff9e7a8da87b80e7f2a5d5c319ce1a2", "text": "GIT Surgeon\nSpirit Main Hospital\nNewark Road\nBrisbane\n\n\n19/12/2019\nRe: Mr Fred Davies\nDear Doctor,\nThank you for urgently admitting Mr Fred Davies, a 65-year-old gentleman gentlman who was\nadmitted to our hospital with symptoms and signs suggestive of possible acute colonic pseudo -\nobstruction and is being transferred transfered to your hospital for further assessment and\ninvestigation.\nToday, Mr Fred presented to our Emergency Department complaining of mild pain related to a\nhugely distended abdomen and associated with lack of appetite and nausea over the past 4\ndays . He reported that last bowel movement was 5 days ago and denied any fever, chills or\nchest pain. However, he reported difficulty in breathing.\nOn examination his vital signs were within normal range except for a tachycardia of 114 beats\nper minute and low saturation of 92% on room air. His abdominal palpation revealed mild\ndiffuse tenderness with no evidence of rebound and guarding.\nHis laboratory findings shows leucocitosis of 14000 and his potassium postassium, BUN               Commented [PQ1]: Leucocytosis (or leukocytosis\nand aspartate aminotransferase were 3.5 , 43 , and 46 respectively repectively. All other\nlaboratory values were unremarkable. Massive colonic dilatation that involves the cecum             Commented [PQ2]: 3.5, 43, and 46 respectively\nsecum, ascending colon and transverse colon was detected on imaging.\nMr Davies has a medical history of hypothyroidism, COPD, hypertension, and hyperlipidemia for\nwhich he takes the following medications: levothyroxine, amlodipine, atrovastatin, albuterol\ninhaler, budesonide, formoterole inhaler. He reported also a surgical history of meniscal tear\nrepair in the right knee.\nIt would be appreciated if you could provide Mr Davies with a surgical assessment and\nabdominopelvic CT scan as you deem appropriate . Should you require further information, do\nnot hesitate to contact me.\nYours sincerely,\nDr M\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                1\n\f\nWriting Feedback    Needs work               Satisfactory                 Good             Excellent\n     Criteria\nPurpose                                                                       \n\nContent                                                                       \n\nConciseness &                                                                 \nClarity\nGenre & Style                                                                  \n\nOrganisation &                                                                \nLayout\nLanguage                                                              \n\nOverall             This is a good effort Mostafa. Well done!\n                    The Name; Address, Date, Salutation and Reference Line are perfect, well done!\nComments\n                    The address is formatted correctly.\n\n                    The word count in the body of the letter is 240 words. Aim for 180-200 in the body of the\n                    text. The body of the text starts after the salutation e.g. “Dear Dr. Jones” and ends before\n                    a generic closing e.g. “Please do not hesitate to contact me if you have any further queries.\n                    It does not include the name of the recipient and the date and the address or the sign off\n                    e.g. “Yours sincerely,”\n\n\n                    There are many issues with spaces. Include a space after commas and full stops.\n                    INCORRECT\n                    Thank you for your help in the matter.Please find test results attached.\n                    CORRECT\n                    Thank you for your help in the matter. Please find test results attached.\n                    INCORRECT\n                    The patient,who is suffering from depression,is unable to shower independently.\n                    CORRECT\n                    The patient, who is suffering from depression, is unable to shower independently.\n\n                    There are some spelling issues.\n\n                    Verb tenses are good.\n\n                    There are some issues with punctuation, grammar and word choice.\n\n                    Practice proofreading your writing and try to give yourself a few minutes to proofread at\n                    the end of the 45 minutes in the exam.\n\n                    Please read the sample letter and compare your letter to it.\n\n                    Review the worksheets in the Grammar and Vocabulary Clinic.\n\n                    Great job!\n\n                    Grade: 360\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                2", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "GIT Surgeon\nSpirit Main Hospital\nNewark Road\nBrisbane\n\n\n19/12/2019\nRe: Mr Fred Davies\nDear Doctor,\nThank you for urgently admitting Mr Fred Davies, a 65-year-old gentleman gentlman who was\nadmitted to our hospital with symptoms and signs suggestive of possible acute colonic pseudo -\nobstruction and is being transferred transfered to your hospital for further assessment and\ninvestigation.\nToday, Mr Fred presented to our Emergency Department complaining of mild pain related to a\nhugely distended abdomen and associated with lack of appetite and nausea over the past 4\ndays . He reported that last bowel movement was 5 days ago and denied any fever, chills or\nchest pain. However, he reported difficulty in breathing.\nOn examination his vital signs were within normal range except for a tachycardia of 114 beats\nper minute and low saturation of 92% on room air. His abdominal palpation revealed mild\ndiffuse tenderness with no evidence of rebound and guarding.\nHis laboratory findings shows leucocitosis of 14000 and his potassium postassium, BUN               Comment